body:
Changes made:
1. Rebase to master commit 215acd52e82f4c575abb715e25e54558deeef998
2. Account for nested tool scripts (scene with tool scripts inside a scene) while generating thumbnails:
 ```
// editor/plugins/editor_preview_plugins.cpp:903
bool EditorPackedScenePreviewPlugin::_remove_scripts_from_packed_scene(Ref<PackedScene> pack) const {
		...

		if (Object::cast_to<PackedScene>(edited_variants[i])) {
			_remove_scripts_from_packed_scene(edited_variants[i]); // Account for nested tool scripts
		}
 ```

Changes made since 5350e36:
1. Rewrite most code for 3d thumbnail creation, now uses a SubViewport node under EditorNode to render thumbnails (Instead of interacting with RenderingServer directly), this should be less prone to bug since all references are auto-freed when removed from EditorNode.
2. Resolved most changes @KoBeWi mentioned
3. Fixed error when scene has ```@export``` variables in scene (Those data are written inside .tscn and will spam error after we remove the scripts, now fixed.)
4. Renamed ```_remove_scripts_from_packed_scene``` to ```_setup_packed_scene``` as it does more than removing scripts  in scene now
5. Implemented a progress bar if generating thumbnails using **gl_compatiblity** renderer (Single-threaded). Delaying a frame between creating thumbnails is not an option, the editor will be next to unresponsive (only 1-2fps), so we wait. This progress bar will be instant if there's only few scenes in queue anyway.
![Screenshot from 2025-04-21 04-31-34](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2eadf21e-c321-448f-ae47-512ba40352fc)
6. Make sure that we only generate thumbnails for a scene at a time, previously there are too many callbacks involved while generating previews, which makes ```EditorResourcePreview::_idle_callback()```and ```EditorResourcePreview::_iterate()``` to be called multiple times while a scene thumbnail is still generating. This is still experimental, I'm still finding a way to deal with large/heavy scenes. Most scenes generates its thumbnail within 1 seconds, but for a large scene it can be over 10 seconds. I think we should skip creating thumbnails for scene that takes more than ~2 seconds and proceed to next scene, unless it's the current opened scene and just been saved (Creating thumbnail for a scene already opened is fast, even sub 1 second for a fairly complex scene). Opened for discussion.
```c++
//editor_resource_preview.cpp::440

	// Ensure to process one item at a time
	singleton->preview_mutex.lock();
	bool processing = singleton->processing_item.path != "";
	int last_msec = singleton->last_process_msec;
	singleton->preview_mutex.unlock();
	if (processing) {
		// Took more than 2 seconds to generate thumbnail, might be stuck or bugged, proceed to next item.
		if (OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_msec() - last_msec > 2000) {
			singleton->preview_mutex.lock();
			singleton->processing_item = QueueItem();
			singleton->preview_mutex.unlock();
		}
		return;
	}
```
---

Issues:
The viewport flickering issue in Mobile Renderer I previously mentioned, turns out it is very likely a renderer bug, it happens when:
1. Renderer is set to Mobile
2. Current opened scene has LightMapGI baked
3. There's a subviewport somewhere (Even outside of MainTree), with a own World3D and a active Camera3D as child

Then the opened scene's LightMapGI will not render. I tried to find ways to workaround but no luck, this should be fixed directly in Mobile renderer. The last resort is to make Mobile Renderer generate thumbnails with Single-Threaded, so the glitch won't appear.

Changes made at commit d0a4299:


1. Make ```EditorNode::add_io_warning()``` able to be called on thread:
```c++
// editor/editor_node.cpp:7139

callable_mp_static(EditorNode::add_io_warning).call_deferred(p_warning);
```
Previously when creating thumbnails outside of main thread, if the scene instantiates with warning, will trigger ```EditorNode:4788:DEVASSERT(Thread::get_caller_id() == Thread::get_main_id())``` and crash.

2. Abort generating thumbnails for scenes that have **Viewport**, **OptionButton** derived class as root, since it'll lead to crashes:
```c++
// editor/plugins/editor_preview_plugins.cpp:344

// Prohibit Viewport class as root when generating thumbnails
bool prohibited_root_type = (
	Object::cast_to<Viewport>(p_scene) || 
	Object::cast_to<OptionButton>(p_scene) // NOTE - OptionButton uses PopupMenu(Derived class of Viewport) internally
);

if (prohibited_root_type) {
	p_scene->queue_free();
	return Ref<Texture2D>();
}
```

3. Do not skip large scene files, instead display file names in progress bar, so users can have clue which file is slowing down:
![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/53703fbf-1d13-4fa1-bae5-5eebde7fbf7d)


4. Fixed **EditorMeshPreviewPlugin**  not generating previews correctly when running on thread by calling ```draw_requester.request_and_wait()``` twice

5. Do not account nodes that are not visible into scene aabb/rect calculation.

6. Tested 2d scene thumbnails, making preview 2d camera as current is necessary if the scene already has another camera, added relevant code back:
```c++
// editor/plugins/editor_preview_plugins.cpp:475

if (EditorResourcePreview::get_singleton()->is_threaded()) {
	callable_mp((Node *)EditorNode::get_singleton(), &Node::add_child).call_deferred(sub_viewport, false, Node::InternalMode::INTERNAL_MODE_DISABLED);
	callable_mp((Camera2D *)camera, &Camera2D::make_current).call_deferred();
} else {
	EditorNode::get_singleton()->add_child(sub_viewport);
	camera->make_current();
}
```

7. Set all **Window** in scene to invisible, avoid popups.
```c++
// editor/plugins/editor_preview_plugins.cpp:584 && 623

// Don't let window to popup
Window *window = Object::cast_to<Window>(p_node);
if (window) {
	window->set_visible(false);
}
```

---

Manual tests done:
1. Tested various projects including the junk file project @KoBeWi provided, with Mobile, Compatibility Renderer, with no crashes (The junk file project is already flooded with loading errors but I see no errors related to thumbnail creation)

2. Can hit play game, exit editor, reimport files, or edit&save scene while preview is still generating without errors. (Mobile Renderer) Need more extensive tests though, if it does run into problem, I'll consider run all thumbnail creation single-threaded for stability.

Changes made since b93e5bff:

Revert the behavior of prohibiting **OptionButton** node as root for the preview scene. See explanation below. 
```c++
// editor/plugins/editor_preview_plugins.cpp:344

	// Prohibit Viewport class as root when generating thumbnails
	if (Object::cast_to<Viewport>(p_scene)) {
		p_scene->queue_free();
		return Ref<Texture2D>();
	}
```


---

@KoBeWi 
> What about other classes with popups? MenuButton, ColorPickerButton etc. EDIT: Actually, if Viewport root is a problem, why OptionButton is also a problem if its popup is not root?

After testing, I confirmed that the crash occurs when there's visible **Window** as scene root and attached to **EditorNode**, but I already added code to set all **Window** to invisible in preparation. So I removed the restriction of **OptionButton** roots and tested it again, the project didn't crash.

EDIT: And to clarify, **Viewport** root does not crash the editor, it's prohibited because when we count 2d/3d nodes in ```EditorPackedScenePreviewPlugin::_count_node_types```, we don't count anything under a Viewport node. If there's a Viewport as scene root, it will cause error. This decision is made because Viewport nodes will mess up how we determine if a scene is 2d/3d (was discussed in this thread, might be collapsed)

> > (The junk file project is already flooded with loading errors but I see no errors related to thumbnail creation)
> 
> Well, the errors are a result of thumbnail generation, but I guess there is no way around that (other than not updating thumbnails 🙃). Although it's not something that will happen in a regular project without random broken files.

Correct, the error log is inevitable since we need to load the .tscn to generate thumbnails for it. Unless we can have a method in **ResourceLoader** to load scene but don't print out any loading errors.

@ChronoDK See the bug report linked above: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102313#issuecomment-2989167627

The long load time is not intentional, it's a bug. So it's not meant to be made configurable, just fixed (or reverted if it can't be fixed easily).

It's not a good practice to work around bugs with settings :)
